			"frameId": null,
			"index": "av",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1111248556,
			"version": 717,
			"versionNonce": 1896664108,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783417844309,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Advantages:  \n    - Protects data integrity by preventing arbitrary out-of-order mutations.\n    - Guarantees immediate access to the most recently cached state change.\n\nCore Academic & System Use Cases:\n    - The Call Stack: The runtime environment (JVM/OS) uses a stack to manage \n    active stack frames, local variables, and return addresses for nested or recursive \n    method executions.\n    - Syntax Parsing: Compilers use stacks to evaluate language delimiters, ensuring \n    matching geometry for parameters and brackets (e.g., {[()]}).\n    - Undo Buffers: Tracking state history sequentially within productivity software \n    like text editors.\n    - Graph Algorithms: Serving as the state-tracking backplane for Depth-First \n    Search (DFS) traversals.",
			"rawText": "Advantages:  \n    - Protects data integrity by preventing arbitrary out-of-order mutations.\n    - Guarantees immediate access to the most recently cached state change.\n\nCore Academic & System Use Cases:\n    - The Call Stack: The runtime environment (JVM/OS) uses a stack to manage \n    active stack frames, local variables, and return addresses for nested or recursive \n    method executions.\n    - Syntax Parsing: Compilers use stacks to evaluate language delimiters, ensuring \n    matching geometry for parameters and brackets (e.g., {[()]}).\n    - Undo Buffers: Tracking state history sequentially within productivity software \n    like text editors.\n    - Graph Algorithms: Serving as the state-tracking backplane for Depth-First \n    Search (DFS) traversals.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Advantages:  \n    - Protects data integrity by preventing arbitrary out-of-order mutations.\n    - Guarantees immediate access to the most recently cached state change.\n\nCore Academic & System Use Cases:\n    - The Call Stack: The runtime environment (JVM/OS) uses a stack to manage \n    active stack frames, local variables, and return addresses for nested or recursive \n    method executions.\n    - Syntax Parsing: Compilers use stacks to evaluate language delimiters, ensuring \n    matching geometry for parameters and brackets (e.g., {[()]}).\n    - Undo Buffers: Tracking state history sequentially within productivity software \n    like text editors.\n    - Graph Algorithms: Serving as the state-tracking backplane for Depth-First \n    Search (DFS) traversals.",
			"autoResize": false,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
