		{
			"id": "sZBOGi2B",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -248.1758290262154,
			"y": 2275.8914360411636,
			"width": 1005.0813168226783,
			"height": 300,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b0T",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 2045341204,
			"version": 1150,
			"versionNonce": 194176532,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783410738313,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Advantages:  \n    - Cleanly decouples data producing components from data consuming systems (asynchronous\n      processing loops).\n    - Enforces predictable chronological equity.\n\nCore Academic & System Use Cases:\n    - Thread/Process Scheduling: Operating system kernels deploy circular scheduling queues\n      (like round-robin selectors) to balance processing resources.\n    - I/O Subsystems: Buffering background operations (e.g., handling print spooling \n      sequences or streaming network data packets).\n    - Graph Traversals: Providing the ordering infrastructure necessary to execute Breadth-\n      First Search (BFS) level-by-level exploration.",
			"rawText": "Advantages:  \n    - Cleanly decouples data producing components from data consuming systems (asynchronous \n      processing loops).\n    - Enforces predictable chronological equity.\n\nCore Academic & System Use Cases:\n    - Thread/Process Scheduling: Operating system kernels deploy circular scheduling queues\n      (like round-robin selectors) to balance processing resources.\n    - I/O Subsystems: Buffering background operations (e.g., handling print spooling \n      sequences or streaming network data packets).\n    - Graph Traversals: Providing the ordering infrastructure necessary to execute Breadth-\n      First Search (BFS) level-by-level exploration.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Advantages:  \n    - Cleanly decouples data producing components from data consuming systems (asynchronous \n      processing loops).\n    - Enforces predictable chronological equity.\n\nCore Academic & System Use Cases:\n    - Thread/Process Scheduling: Operating system kernels deploy circular scheduling queues\n      (like round-robin selectors) to balance processing resources.\n    - I/O Subsystems: Buffering background operations (e.g., handling print spooling \n      sequences or streaming network data packets).\n    - Graph Traversals: Providing the ordering infrastructure necessary to execute Breadth-\n      First Search (BFS) level-by-level exploration.",
			"autoResize": false,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
