			"versionNonce": 1565680172,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783410699630,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "The Proof: By preserving tracking variables at opposite boundaries (front for deletion, back\nfor insertion), we bypass sequential list iteration entirely. \nAdding an element requires updating the current back.next pointer, and removing an element\nshifts the front pointer one memory increment forward. \nBoth operations execute independently of sequence size, completing in constant O(1) time.",
			"rawText": "The Proof: By preserving tracking variables at opposite boundaries (front for deletion, back for insertion), we bypass sequential list iteration entirely. \nAdding an element requires updating the current back.next pointer, and removing an element shifts the front pointer one memory increment forward. \nBoth operations execute independently of sequence size, completing in constant O(1) time.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": "d-GXIgVirDTwIlInQFLMD",
			"originalText": "The Proof: By preserving tracking variables at opposite boundaries (front for deletion, back for insertion), we bypass sequential list iteration entirely. \nAdding an element requires updating the current back.next pointer, and removing an element shifts the front pointer one memory increment forward. \nBoth operations execute independently of sequence size, completing in constant O(1) time.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
