		{
			"id": "8tbE8HFa",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 1966.2107418331439,
			"y": 533.7579435676217,
			"width": 998.6644620720025,
			"height": 225,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b1B",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1763272108,
			"version": 311,
			"versionNonce": 244480788,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783415151503,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "1. Read the expression sequence character by character from left to right.\n2. If an open grouping token is recognized ((, [, {), pass it directly to the tracking\nstack via push().\n3. If a close grouping token is encountered, immediately verify if the stack is empty. \n   An empty stack indicates a closure without an origin point, violating balance rules.\n4. Pop the current element from the top of the stack and check for symmetry. \n   If the types do not match, fail immediately.\n5. Upon evaluating all characters, complete balance is confirmed only if the tracking \n   stack has been completely cleared.",
			"rawText": "1. Read the expression sequence character by character from left to right.\n2. If an open grouping token is recognized ((, [, {), pass it directly to the tracking stack via push().\n3. If a close grouping token is encountered, immediately verify if the stack is empty. \n   An empty stack indicates a closure without an origin point, violating balance rules.\n4. Pop the current element from the top of the stack and check for symmetry. \n   If the types do not match, fail immediately.\n5. Upon evaluating all characters, complete balance is confirmed only if the tracking \n   stack has been completely cleared.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "1. Read the expression sequence character by character from left to right.\n2. If an open grouping token is recognized ((, [, {), pass it directly to the tracking stack via push().\n3. If a close grouping token is encountered, immediately verify if the stack is empty. \n   An empty stack indicates a closure without an origin point, violating balance rules.\n4. Pop the current element from the top of the stack and check for symmetry. \n   If the types do not match, fail immediately.\n5. Upon evaluating all characters, complete balance is confirmed only if the tracking \n   stack has been completely cleared.",
			"autoResize": false,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
