			"updated": 1783415934284,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Procedural Rules:",
			"rawText": "Procedural Rules:",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Procedural Rules:",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
		{
			"id": "daJ9XwK1",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 865.2004264111009,
			"y": 2485.42515703192,
			"width": 1000.9987182617188,
			"height": 250,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b29",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 16574636,
			"version": 197,
			"versionNonce": 1064427540,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783416234389,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "1. Operands (Numbers/Letters): Send immediately to the Postfix Output string.\n2. Open Parenthesis (: Push immediately onto the Operator Stack.\n3. Close Parenthesis ): Pop operators off the stack and append them to the Output string \n   until an open parenthesis ( is encountered. Pop and discard the open parenthesis.\n4. Operators (+, -, x, /, etc.): Pop operators off the stack to the Output string if they \n   have greater than or equal precedence to the current operator. Stop when encountering a \n   lower precedence operator or an open parenthesis, then push the current operator onto \n   the stack.\n5. EOF: When the string is fully parsed, pop all remaining operators from the stack to the \n   Output string.",
			"rawText": "1. Operands (Numbers/Letters): Send immediately to the Postfix Output string.\n2. Open Parenthesis (: Push immediately onto the Operator Stack.\n3. Close Parenthesis ): Pop operators off the stack and append them to the Output string \n   until an open parenthesis ( is encountered. Pop and discard the open parenthesis.\n4. Operators (+, -, x, /, etc.): Pop operators off the stack to the Output string if they \n   have greater than or equal precedence to the current operator. Stop when encountering a \n   lower precedence operator or an open parenthesis, then push the current operator onto \n   the stack.\n5. EOF: When the string is fully parsed, pop all remaining operators from the stack to the \n   Output string.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "1. Operands (Numbers/Letters): Send immediately to the Postfix Output string.\n2. Open Parenthesis (: Push immediately onto the Operator Stack.\n3. Close Parenthesis ): Pop operators off the stack and append them to the Output string \n   until an open parenthesis ( is encountered. Pop and discard the open parenthesis.\n4. Operators (+, -, x, /, etc.): Pop operators off the stack to the Output string if they \n   have greater than or equal precedence to the current operator. Stop when encountering a \n   lower precedence operator or an open parenthesis, then push the current operator onto \n   the stack.\n5. EOF: When the string is fully parsed, pop all remaining operators from the stack to the \n   Output string.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
