		},
		{
			"id": "yL94v7Vg",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 864.6309305346739,
			"y": 3533.268483532981,
			"width": 995.2607667815876,
			"height": 275,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b2L",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 420537748,
			"version": 409,
			"versionNonce": 1896925740,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783416337314,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "1. Scan the Postfix string from left to right.\n2. If the token is a number, push it onto the Operand Stack.\n3. If the token is an operator, pop the top two numbers from the stack.\n4. Execute the mathematical operation. \n    CRITICAL EXAM BOUNDARY: The first popped element is the right operand (operand2), \n    and the second popped element is the left operand (operand1).\n\n        Result = operand1 [operator] operand2\n\n5. Push the calculated result back onto the stack.\n6. The final value remaining on the stack at EOF is the global solution.",
			"rawText": "1. Scan the Postfix string from left to right.\n2. If the token is a number, push it onto the Operand Stack.\n3. If the token is an operator, pop the top two numbers from the stack.\n4. Execute the mathematical operation. \n    CRITICAL EXAM BOUNDARY: The first popped element is the right operand (operand2), \n    and the second popped element is the left operand (operand1).\n\n        Result = operand1 [operator] operand2\n\n5. Push the calculated result back onto the stack.\n6. The final value remaining on the stack at EOF is the global solution.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "1. Scan the Postfix string from left to right.\n2. If the token is a number, push it onto the Operand Stack.\n3. If the token is an operator, pop the top two numbers from the stack.\n4. Execute the mathematical operation. \n    CRITICAL EXAM BOUNDARY: The first popped element is the right operand (operand2), \n    and the second popped element is the left operand (operand1).\n\n        Result = operand1 [operator] operand2\n\n5. Push the calculated result back onto the stack.\n6. The final value remaining on the stack at EOF is the global solution.",
			"autoResize": false,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
